"""Sparse surface-syntax rules for entry points and source documentation.

The name 'main' is strongly negative after a function-declaration keyword.
Unindented comments after definitions are also negative, especially in Go;
quoted/escaped code and numbered listings have weaker responses. These are
surface cues, not a full parser. Small document-opening and dot-divider rules
capture a few additional formatting effects. Two small rules recognize Mizar
variable declarations and pointer return types. Other tokens get zero.
