"""A local spelling detector for i/y followed by another vowel.

The negative response is strongest for fragmented spellings like i-a-C,
where C begins the following token. It also responds to ia, ie, io and iu
inside a fragment. Transliteration makes the same rules apply to several
alphabets. Common grammatical endings weaken the boundary response.
These are approximate spelling rules, not a dictionary of token identities.
"""
